# GitHub to GitLab Migration & Backup Tool

This repository provides a powerful, real-time Python synchronization script designed to migrate and backup your GitHub repositories to a private GitLab account. 

## Features
- **0MB Data Server-to-Server Import:** Leverages direct GitHub-to-GitLab API imports when possible, effectively migrating repositories using 0MB of your own data bandwidth!
- **4G/5G Mobile Data Detector:** Automatically detects if you are running on a mobile network (4G/LTE) and smartly pauses or prompts before executing data-heavy operations.
- **Real-Time Terminal Interface:** Uses the `rich` Python library to render gorgeous progress bars. It reads byte-level output from Git to update clone, update, and push operations in real-time.
- **Resilient Execution:** If a specific repository gets locked by Windows or fails to clone (e.g. `Permission denied` errors), the script catches the error, skips the repository, cleans up, and safely moves to the next one without crashing.
- **Automatic Private Mirrors:** Creates private repositories on your GitLab account dynamically via the GitLab CLI.
- **Incremental Syncing:** Re-running the script will only fetch the latest changes for already cloned repositories rather than re-downloading everything, saving bandwidth and time.

